# Architecture hardening plan

This checklist is the implementation source of truth for the architectural
improvements identified after the UI component encapsulation work. The goal is
to finish the ownership boundaries introduced by that refactor, reduce the
responsibility of `ui/main_window.lua`, and make future reusable-widget and
responsive-layout work safer.

This is a behavior-preserving refactor. It must not redesign SoulSearch,
silently change persistence, or complete unrelated feature items from
`docs/project.todo`.

Update this document as each phase lands. Record focused and full validation in
the Execution evidence table instead of marking a gate complete from code
inspection alone.

## Target architecture

- [ ] `FilterPanel` constructs and owns its complete widget subtree as an
      actual `ModalPanelWindow`-derived class; no factory owns the class
      implementation outside `FilterPanel:init()`.
- [ ] Main Window communicates with Filter, Results, and Stats components only
      through documented component APIs rather than republished descendant
      views.
- [ ] Filter-editor transient state cannot represent multiple simultaneously
      active pickers.
- [ ] Pure presenters build filter, preset, and result display models without
      reading or mutating widgets.
- [x] A pure search-session boundary owns search/filter/scope/sort state while
      Main Window remains the DFHack widget and I/O coordinator.
- [x] Results and Stats use one reusable sort-state/header/list architecture
      after evaluating applicable built-in DFHack widgets.
- [ ] UI tests use a small, consistent script/widget harness instead of many
      subtly different fake class implementations.
- [ ] Clean reload adds only the behavior DFHack does not provide natively:
      old-screen teardown, stale-definition cleanup, coherent reconstruction,
      contract validation, and overlay rescan.
- [ ] Fortress/map availability policy has one implementation owner.
- [ ] Feature-driven Unit Info and responsive-panel work builds on these
      component boundaries instead of reopening them.

## Architectural constraints

- [ ] Preserve all public command, bootstrap, `ui.open()`, `ui.dismiss_all()`,
      multi-window, scoped-window, reload, and control-panel contracts.
- [ ] Preserve current default-hotkey behavior: claim `Ctrl-F` only when the
      live binding is unoccupied and never replace another command's binding.
- [ ] Preserve view behavior, geometry, focus order, keys, labels, colors,
      hitboxes, tooltips, selection retention, refresh order, and lifecycle
      semantics unless a separately approved feature explicitly changes one.
- [ ] Keep session-only window settings session-only; do not introduce hidden
      marker files or persistent opt-out state.
- [ ] Prefer DFHack's native changed-script `reqscript()` reload behavior for
      ordinary edits; do not build a parallel general-purpose module loader.
- [ ] Keep dialogs, printing, filesystem access, DFHack map actions, and raw
      game access outside pure state and presenter modules.
- [ ] Keep functional value/policy modules functional. Do not turn
      `filter_state`, sort-state helpers, candidate providers, catalogs, or
      formatting utilities into classes without mutable identity or lifecycle.
- [ ] Do not introduce a service locator, event bus, generic repository layer,
      dependency-injection framework, or generic world-context container.
- [ ] Prefer one cohesive module over many one-function files.
- [ ] Add focused component or pure-module tests before migrating broad
      characterization behavior.

## Explicitly separate feature work

- [ ] Do not add Animals scope, change picker selection/close behavior, alter
      button copy/padding, or change tooltip chrome in this refactor.
- [ ] Do not implement creatures-menu integration or new scoped-window launch
      affordances in this refactor.
- [ ] Do not implement Divider/ResizingPanel behavior until the responsive
      integration phase explicitly begins.
- [ ] Do not decompose Unit Info solely to increase file count; perform that
      split when the Stats popover creates a concrete reuse boundary.
- [ ] Do not mark corresponding `docs/project.todo` feature items complete
      until their own behavior and live validation are finished.

## Phase 0 - Baseline and ownership characterization

- [x] Record the clean/dirty worktree state and preserve unrelated changes.
- [x] Record current source size and responsibility baselines for:
  - [x] `ui/main_window.lua` imports, methods, and state fields;
  - [x] `ui/filter_panel.lua` constructor/factory responsibilities;
  - [x] `ui_format.lua` consumers and function groups;
  - [x] `tests/support/soulsearch_env.lua` loaders and widget stubs; and
  - [x] `module_registry.lua` entries and asserted reconstruction order.
- [x] Add or confirm focused characterization for:
  - [x] direct Filter Panel construction and child order;
  - [x] picker exclusivity and close transitions;
  - [x] Main Window use of component APIs;
  - [x] result and filter selection across refreshes;
  - [x] Results and Stats sort cycles, hitboxes, and persistence; and
  - [x] edited-module reload with open and dismissed windows.
- [x] Document the intended ownership boundary before moving code:
  - [x] widgets own their subviews and transient view state;
  - [x] presenters own display-model construction;
  - [x] the search session owns domain/search interaction state;
  - [x] Main Window binds widgets to the session and external adapters; and
  - [x] Main Screen owns screen registration and teardown.

### Recorded baseline - 2026-07-14

- Worktree was clean before Phase 0 edits; this phase changes only its
  characterization test and this plan.
- `ui/main_window.lua`: 1,109 lines, 39,323 bytes, 21 internal imports, and
  57 `SoulSearchWindow` methods. It currently initializes rows/results,
  queries, result sort, six Filter Panel/picker booleans, scope, descriptors,
  and filter state, then also coordinates persistence, presenters, and DFHack
  actions.
- `ui/filter_panel.lua`: 289 lines, 8 class methods, and 3 factories. The
  `create()` factory currently owns the composite child-tree construction,
  while `FilterPanel:init()` stores inputs and choice state.
- `ui_format.lua`: 310 lines, 21 functions, and 5 direct module consumers. It
  mixes shared text helpers with Filter, preset, Results, and Stats display
  transformations.
- `tests/support/soulsearch_env.lua`: 1,230 lines and 39 `load_*` helpers,
  including several purpose-specific widget/class stubs.
- `module_registry.lua`: 44 listed modules; `module_registry_test.lua` has 31
  explicit reconstruction-order assertions. The registry remains a flat clean
  reload manifest, not a dependency graph.
- Existing focused suites cover direct Filter Panel construction/order, result
  selection retention, Results and Stats sorting/hitboxes/persistence, and
  reload teardown. This phase adds real picker close/exclusivity transitions
  and Main Window component-delegation characterization.
- Ownership after the planned refactor is: widgets own subviews and transient
  view state; presenters own display snapshots; SearchSession owns pure
  search/filter/scope/sort state; Main Window binds widgets, external adapters,
  and refresh; Main Screen owns screen registration and teardown.

### Phase 0 gate

- [x] No production implementation has moved.
- [x] Focused characterization passes against the pre-refactor architecture.
- [x] `tools/Build.ps1`, `tools/Test.ps1`, and `git diff --check` pass.

## Phase 1 - Make Filter Panel fully class-owned

- [x] Move the widget-tree construction currently owned by
      `filter_panel.create()` into `FilterPanel:init()`.
- [x] Instantiate the component directly as `FilterPanel{...}` from Main
      Window.
- [x] Move constructor normalization such as initial unit-scope label
      resolution into the class.
- [x] Remove the `create()` compatibility factory after every consumer and
      test uses the class constructor.
- [x] Retain trivial one-purpose leaf factories for the external Edit button
      and active-filter count unless they acquire independent state or
      lifecycle behavior.
- [x] Tighten picker constructor contracts:
  - [x] remove duplicated or unused `window_id`, title, and visibility fields;
  - [x] put widget attributes on the widget rather than duplicating them in
        callback/input tables; and
  - [x] keep only callbacks and domain payloads actually consumed by each
        picker class.
- [x] Add focused tests proving that `FilterPanel:init()` owns the same child
      IDs, order, frames, keys, callbacks, visibility, and paint order.
- [x] Update the module registry contract only if an obsolete factory contract
      is currently asserted.

### Phase 1 gate

- [x] `FilterPanel` is the only implementation owner of its composite tree.
- [x] No production or test consumer calls `filter_panel.create()`.
- [x] Trivial leaf factories remain stateless and local to their owning
      module.
- [x] Filter Panel focused tests and broad UI characterization pass.
- [x] `tools/Build.ps1`, `tools/Test.ps1`, and `git diff --check` pass.

## Phase 2 - Enforce component APIs and consolidate transient UI state

- [x] Add narrow Filter Panel APIs for every remaining legitimate host action,
      including selected-filter lookup, picker visibility/state transitions,
      focus operations, choice updates, and tooltip resolution.
- [x] Migrate Main Window away from direct descendant access, including the
      active `filter_list` selection path.
- [x] Migrate characterization tests that reach through Main Window into
      Filter Panel focused tests or host-facing API assertions.
- [x] Delete recursive descendant republishing from Main Window once no
      production consumer depends on it.
- [x] Replace the picker boolean matrix with one exclusive state:
  - [x] define the allowed picker values (`attribute`, `skill`, `race`,
        `scope`, `preset`, or none);
  - [x] make open, toggle, close, and panel-dismiss transitions explicit;
  - [x] make invalid simultaneous-picker states unrepresentable; and
  - [x] preserve current query text and picker selection behavior.
- [x] Prefer Filter Panel ownership of transient picker state. Use a small
      pure `filter_editor_state.lua` value module only if the transitions need
      independent reuse or testing.
- [x] Remove `is_*_picker_open`, `on_toggle_*`, and `on_close_*` callback pairs
      that exist only because Main Window currently owns component state.
- [x] Retain domain-changing callbacks for filters, scope, and presets.
- [x] Add a transition-table test covering every picker-to-picker,
      picker-to-list, close, and panel-dismiss path.

### Phase 2 gate

- [x] Main Window accesses only direct children and documented component APIs.
- [x] No recursive descendant aliases exist at the Main Window root.
- [x] At most one Filter Panel picker can be active.
- [x] The Filter Panel host contract is materially narrower than the previous
