### Phase 6 gate

- [ ] UI tests construct classes through one consistent minimal widget model.
- [ ] No migrated loader carries a private incompatible class implementation.
- [ ] Missing fake dependencies fail explicitly.
- [ ] Fortress/map availability has one implementation owner.
- [ ] The full pure-Lua suite passes without weakening assertions.
- [ ] `tools/Build.ps1`, `tools/Test.ps1`, and `git diff --check` pass.

## Phase 7 - Simplify and validate clean reload

- [ ] Record the native DFHack behavior this phase must not duplicate:
  - [ ] `reqscript()` reloads an individual changed script on the next import;
  - [ ] normal reload preserves the script environment, so changed and added
        definitions update without clearing unrelated consumers; and
  - [ ] `defclass()` updates an existing class table when the environment has
        not been cleared.
- [ ] Record the stronger clean-reload cases SoulSearch intentionally owns:
  - [ ] removed or renamed globals/methods must not remain in an old script
        environment;
  - [ ] open widget instances must be dismissed and reconstructed so `init()`
        rebuilds their child trees and callbacks;
  - [ ] direct cached dependency members must not mix old and new module
        generations after an environment clear; and
  - [ ] the overlay script must be rediscovered through `overlay.rescan()`.
- [ ] Do not add `depends_on` metadata, topological sorting, cycle detection, or
      a general dependency-graph framework.
- [ ] Retain a flat owned-module manifest only if it remains necessary to clear
      every SoulSearch script environment during a clean reload.
- [ ] Keep the existing dependency-before-consumer order explicit in that flat
      manifest while environment clearing requires deterministic forward
      reconstruction.
- [ ] Keep contract name/type validation as a lightweight post-reconstruction
      guard.
- [ ] Ensure the reload coordinator has one implementation of each required
      step:
  - [ ] dismiss old SoulSearch screens;
  - [ ] clear stale SoulSearch script environments;
  - [ ] reconstruct the flat manifest in its documented order;
  - [ ] invalidate/rescan the overlay through the required DFHack mechanism;
        and
  - [ ] prepare lifecycle caches and the claim-if-free keybinding afterward.
- [ ] Remove redundant clearing, loading, or registry reconstruction passes if
      focused tests demonstrate that fewer passes still produce one clean
      generation.
- [ ] Exercise both native and clean reload scenarios:
  - [ ] changed function body and added definition through native `reqscript()`;
  - [ ] removed definition through `soulsearch reload`;
  - [ ] changed component child tree with a window already open;
  - [ ] changed dependency member cached by an unchanged consumer;
  - [ ] reload with no open windows and with multiple open windows; and
  - [ ] changed overlay definition followed by rescan.

### Phase 7 gate

- [ ] Ordinary changed-file reload relies on native DFHack behavior.
- [ ] Clean reload dismisses old screens and reconstructs one coherent module
      generation without stale deleted definitions.
- [ ] The reload coordinator uses no dependency graph or general-purpose
      loader abstraction.
- [ ] The flat manifest and explicit order contain only information required by
      the retained clean-reload implementation.
- [ ] Contract validation and overlay rescan still run after reconstruction.
- [ ] `tools/Build.ps1`, `tools/Test.ps1`, and `git diff --check` pass.

## Phase 8 - Perform integration-driven component decomposition

This phase coordinates existing `docs/project.todo` items. It must not mark
those feature items complete merely because component files exist.

- [ ] Begin Unit Info decomposition when the Stats popover needs a smaller
      reusable component than the full current panel.
- [ ] Confirm final naming and responsibility before renaming the existing
      Stats panel to `UnitInfoPanel`.
- [ ] Extract cohesive reusable widgets only where there is a real consumer:
  - [ ] `UnitIdentity` for name/title/profession presentation;
  - [ ] `MatchedFiltersPanel` for matched-filter title and rows; and
  - [ ] `UnitStatsList` for stat columns, records, scrolling, sorting, and
        tooltips.
- [ ] Compose the full Unit Info panel from those widgets.
- [ ] Make the popover consume `UnitStatsList` when it intentionally excludes
      identity or matched-filter content.
- [ ] Preserve shared Stats subject and presenter contracts rather than
      copying row construction into each host.
- [ ] Start Divider/ResizingPanel work only after hosts no longer depend on
      descendant aliases or hard-coded component internals.
- [ ] Keep responsive layout policy outside domain/session modules.
- [ ] Add component-specific tests and perform live layout checks at minimum,
      typical, and large window sizes.

### Phase 8 gate

- [ ] Each extracted Unit Info widget has at least two justified consumers or
      one clear independent lifecycle/reuse boundary.
- [ ] Main window and popover compose shared widgets without copied
      implementations.
- [ ] Responsive hosts use documented layout/component APIs.
- [ ] Related `docs/project.todo` items reflect actual feature completion and
      live validation.
- [ ] `tools/Build.ps1`, `tools/Test.ps1`, and `git diff --check` pass.

## Phase 9 - Automated, packaged, reload, and live closure

- [ ] Run separately and record:
  - [ ] `tools/Build.ps1`;
  - [ ] `tools/Test.ps1`;
  - [ ] `tools/Publish.ps1`;
  - [ ] `tools/VerifyPackage.ps1` against the produced archive; and
  - [ ] `git diff --check`.
- [ ] Verify the package contains every new runtime module and no deleted
      compatibility module or duplicate implementation.
- [ ] Run edited-module reload checks across every architectural layer.
- [ ] Run a fortress-mode smoke pass covering:
  - [ ] default and scoped window open/close/reopen;
  - [ ] multiple independent windows;
  - [ ] Filter Panel and every exclusive picker transition;
  - [ ] filter add/remove/direction/priority/clear and preset workflows;
  - [ ] unit-scope changes and candidate refresh;
  - [ ] query, result selection retention, navigation, sorting, and zoom;
  - [ ] Stats sorting, scrolling, and tooltips;
  - [ ] window drag, resize, persistence, and teardown; and
  - [ ] reload with windows open and after all windows are dismissed.
- [ ] Confirm control-panel discoverability and claim-if-free `Ctrl-F`
      bootstrap behavior remain intact.
- [ ] Review `git diff -- docs/project.todo` and confirm only intentionally
      completed feature items changed.

### Phase 9 gate

- [ ] Pure state, presenters, widgets, clean-reload coordinator, package, and
      live UI behavior all validate their respective boundaries.
- [ ] Automated, package, reload, and live observations are recorded
      separately.
- [ ] No compatibility alias, duplicate presenter, duplicate sort transition,
      or parallel component implementation remains.

## Definition of done

- [ ] `FilterPanel` directly owns construction and transient state for its
      widget subtree.
- [ ] Main Window has no recursive descendant exposure and uses only component
      APIs.
- [ ] Main Window no longer owns display-model loops or pure search-session
      transitions.
- [ ] Results and Stats share one tested sort/list/header architecture.
- [ ] `ui_format.lua` contains only genuinely cohesive shared formatting
      behavior.
- [ ] UI test environments use one consistent minimal class/widget harness.
- [ ] Clean reload complements native `reqscript()` behavior through a minimal
      flat manifest and contains no dependency-graph framework.
- [ ] Fortress/map availability has one owner.
- [ ] Unit Info and responsive feature work composes these boundaries without
      duplicated implementations.
- [ ] Public behavior, lifecycle, persistence, bootstrap, and control-panel
      integration remain intact.
- [ ] Build, tests, package verification, whitespace checks, reload checks, and
      live smoke validation are green with recorded evidence.

